    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-040: Border Shorthand Expansion** — parse-time expansion of `border: <width> <style> <color>` and per-side forms. **Documentation only.** Implementation (2 commits, ~80-100 lines, parse-side only) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\n**The problem**: ADR-012 expands `margin`, `padding`, `border-width` but *not* the 3-token `border` shorthand. Every Wikipedia element styled with `border: 1px solid X` currently has **no visible border**. ADR-039's box-model work surfaced this during test-fix; ADR-040 closes it.\n\n## Measured on Wikipedia CSS (2026-10-28)\n\n| Form | Uses | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| `border: <width> <style> <color>` (3-token) | **23** | `1px solid #a2a9b1` |\n| `border: 0` | **26** | `border: 0` |\n| Per-side `border-top/right/bottom/left` | **8** | `1px solid transparent` |\n| Standalone `border-width` (already works) | 7 | — |\n| Standalone `border-color` (invisible w/o width) | 63 | — |\n| Standalone `border-style` (invisible w/o width) | 4 | — |\n\n**131 border-related declarations** — 57 of which are the shorthand forms that currently produce nothing.\n\n## First-viewport impact (viewport 1774)\n\n| Element | Border declaration | Visible effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| `form.cdx-search-input` | `border: 1px solid #a2a9b1` | **Search field gains 1px gray border** |\n| `h1#firstHeading` | `border-bottom: 1px solid #a2a9b1` | **Article title gains bottom underline** |\n| `div.vector-column-start` | `border-top: 1px solid transparent` | Transparent — no visual |\n| `div.vector-column-end` | `border-top: 1px solid transparent` | Transparent — no visual |\n\n**2 genuinely visible first-viewport changes.** Both correct per real Wikipedia. First-viewport PNG will differ — that's the delta, measurable and verifiable.\n\n## What the ADR specifies\n\n### Parse-time expansion (per ADR-012's existing pattern)\n\n- `border: <width> <style> <color>` → `border-width` + `border-style` + `border-color` (3 longhands at same specificity/importance)\n- `border: 0` → `border-width: 0`\n- `border: none` → `border-width: 0`\n- `border: <width> none <color>` → `border-width: 0` (CSS spec §8.5.3)\n- `border: <width> <color>` (2-token) → width + color, style defaults to none → invisible per CSS spec *(documented deviation from current paint-path behavior for this form only; 0 uses in target)*\n- `border-top/right/bottom/left: <width> <style> <color>` → 3 per-side longhands\n- `border-top/right/bottom/left: 0` → `border-<side>-width: 0`\n- `!important` preserved through expansion\n- Malformed forms drop the rule\n\n### Zero layout/paint changes\n\nLayout already reads `box.border[i]` from `border-width` longhand. Paint already draws borders from `LayoutBox::border` + `border_color`. Once `border: 1px solid X` expands to `border-width: 1px`, layout picks it up automatically. **Pure cascade/parse fix.**\n\n### `border-style: none` zeroes width\n\nPer CSS spec §8.5.3, the expansion reads the style token and conditionally emits `border-width: 0` when style is `none`. Otherwise paint would draw a rectangle where the browser draws nothing.\n\n## Deferred (7 items, all enumerated in ADR)\n\n- **`border-style: dashed | dotted` renders solid** — paint-side change (Cairo dash), 0 uses in target page\n- **`border-radius`** — needs Cairo arc support, own ADR\n- **`border-collapse` / `border-spacing`** — table category\n- **`parent_content_height` threading** → **ADR-041** — 5 uses, zero visible delta, signature churn\n- **`overflow: auto | scroll` subsystem** → **ADR-042** — 4 uses, needs nested-overflow infrastructure (detection, scrollbar paint, wheel routing), ~150-250 lines\n- **`aspect-ratio`** — 0 uses, deferred indefinitely\n- **`border: <width> <color>` 2-token** renders solid instead of invisible — documented CSS-spec deviation, 0 uses\n\n## ADR-039 lesson codified\n\nADR-039 Commit 2 (`box-sizing: border-box`) shipped, was **reverted** (`769afb5`), and is now recorded honestly (`b9dce37`). ADR-040's Verification section codifies the lesson:\n\n> **Render and inspect PNG before merge** — ADR-039's lesson codified. Any visible border appearing where it shouldn't (e.g. on body, on the header itself) must be caught before merge.\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\n- [ ] **2 visible first-viewport changes accepted** — search field border + heading underline. Both present on real Wikipedia. PNG delta is the verification method.\n- [ ] **`border-style: dashed | dotted` renders solid** — 0 uses in target page. Comfortable deferring paint-side dashes?\n- [ ] **`border: <width> <color>` 2-token deviation** — documented CSS-spec deviation for the 2-token form only (renders solid instead of invisible). 0 uses in target page. Acceptable?\n- [ ] **`parent_content_height` split to ADR-041** — the ADR explicitly argues for this split (mixed-risk bundle pattern from ADR-039). Agree?\n- [ ] **`overflow: auto | scroll` split to ADR-042** — same reasoning; needs scroll subsystem. Agree?\n- [ ] **PNG-before-merge discipline** — ADR-039 was reverted because it shipped mixed-risk without PNG inspection. ADR-040 commits to PNG inspection on the implementation branch.\n\n## Test plan\n\nNo code touched, so no test changes. After merge, run `cmake --build build && ./build/tests/honeybee_tests` to confirm `main` still clean (494 cases, 1881 assertions, unchanged).\n\n## ADR\n\n`docs/decisions/040-border-shorthand.md` — status Accepted; implementation in follow-up PR.\n\nRefs #203\n",
